Sequence [drop-down list] - DismantleStation
Select how the DismantleStation distributes the dismantled MUs to its successors.
Remarks
You can select one of these settings:
• MUs to all Successors:
◦ Select Create MUs from the drop-down list Dismantle Mode, to make the DismantleStation create a
new MU for each successor and moves that MU there.
The DismantleStation moves the main MU to the successor, whose number you typed into the text
box Main MU to Successor with Number.
◦ Select Detach MUs from the drop-down list Dismantle Mode, to make the DismantleStation move
the MUs to each successor in turn, except for the successor that receives the main MU.
The DismantleStation moves the main MU to the successor, whose number you typed into the text
box Main MU to Successor with Number.
If the DismantleStation has four successors for example, and if it moves the main MU on to successor
number 2, it will pass the new MU on to successors number 1, 3, and 4. It moves the main MU to the
successor with the number 2.
For these settings you have to fill out the Dismantle Table:
• MUs exiting independent of other MUs: TheDismantleStation attempts to move the main MU, and
after that each MU on to the successor you defined, as soon as possible.
• Main MU after other MUs: The DismantleStation first moves the mounting parts on to the successor,
and then the main MU.
If you only want to unload those mounting parts from the main part, which you type into the Dismantle
Table, select MUs exiting independent of other MUs or Main MU after other MUs and the Dismantle
Sequence [drop-down list] - DismantleStation
Plant Simulation Help 11-1823
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

mode > Detach MUs. Always type a valid MU class into the column MU and a positive number into the
column Number.
